  "summary": "Messages queue cleared (6 items):\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG, handled first: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while taking apixaban and naproxen. Sent a stat task to RN triage (task-t0001) and an urgent message telling her to go to the ED now (comm-t0002).\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg: her last BMP (2025-09-08) is more than 12 months old, and she had a visit 2026-03-17. Sent a 30-day supply with 0 refills, replacing the old order (mr-t0004). Ordered a BMP (sr-t0005) and told the patient.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin: conflicts with the chart. The 2026-08-11 St. Brigid cardiology consult stopped atorvastatin for muscle aches and started rosuvastatin 10 mg, but atorvastatin is still listed as active. Did not refill and did not change the regimen. Created a task for you as PCP to sort out his statin list (task-t0008, focus mr-t6-atorvastatin) and told the patient.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), Dr. Reyes's request for amoxicillin-clavulanate: NOT ordered. An outside urgent-care note from 2024-03-09 shows anaphylaxis to Augmentin (hives, lip and throat swelling, treated with epinephrine). Recorded the allergy as unconfirmed with high criticality (alg-t0011) and marked the NKDA entry inactive. Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg twice daily for 5-7 days (comm-t0013). I am not allowed to place the alternative, and Reyes's prescribing credentials are still pending, so an urgent task asks you to decide on the antibiotic today (task-t0014). Wrote a chart note (doc-t0015).\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin: HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62, both from 2026-07-15. Renewed metformin 1000 mg twice daily for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0017) and told the patient.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031): his request for a November blood pressure check (mornings preferred) went to the scheduling pool as a task (task-t0020). Told the patient.\nAll inbox items are closed and linked to these actions.",
